  {"second":8,"mapSize":340288,"retainedAncestryNodes":1585710,"maxChainDepth":1245426,"rssMB":699}

  mapSize plateaus (~340–390K) while retainedAncestryNodes grows linearly and a single .previous chain reaches
  ~1.24M deep. With the default old-space size, this OOMs a bare Node process in ~36 s.

  Note on async_hooks destroy (ruling out the obvious explanation)

  A separate async_hooks probe on Node v22.21.1 showed destroy firing for 800,009 of 800,013 promise resources
  (≈100%), so this is not "destroy never fires." Eviction works; the retention is via .previous/.awaited strong
  references pinned by a long-lived live entry, not stuck Map entries.

