### Repro steps

When writing code like this,
```js
// option 1: import as `useIsChromatic` to memoize the `ref`
import getIsChromatic from 'chromatic/isChromatic';
import classnames from 'classnames';
import React from 'react';
import { useResizeDetector } from 'react-resize-detector';

export const SomeComponent = ({ className }) => {
  // option 2: move outside the function to memoize the `ref`
  const isChromatic = getIsChromatic();

  const { ref: resizeRef } = useResizeDetector();

  return (
    <div
      ref={(node) => {
        resizeRef(node);
        // option 3: comment out to memoize the `ref`
        if (!isChromatic) {/* ... */}
      }}
      className={classnames('xxx-monaco-editor-pane w-full', className,
        // option 4: comment out to memoize the `ref` above
        { 'overflow-auto p-2': isChromatic, }
      )}
    >
      foo
    </div>
  );
};
```
the `ref` is not getting memoized, it just gets moved out:
```js
  const t1 = (node) => {
    resizeRef(node);

    if (!isChromatic) {
    }
  };
```

When following one of the four options laid out in the comments, the code becomes correctly memoized:
```js
  let t1;
  if ($[0] !== resizeRef) {
    t1 = (node) => {
      resizeRef(node);

      if (!isChromatic) {
      }
    };
    $[0] = resizeRef;
    $[1] = t1;
  } else {
    t1 = $[1];
  }
```

This is very arbitrary and in our case led to thousands of rerenders due to the non-stable callback that were - thanks to the compiler - sub-1-ms, but still problematic.

